review:
-A lot of server lag;
-Can't trade with the rest of people if you don't pay for a premium account;
-If you pay for a premium account, you can trade 30 TIMES PER MONTH!
-A lot of basic MMO systems are restricted to avoid gold sellers (thus punishing the players) and.. guess what? It DOESN'T avoid gold sellers! They're everywhere in the game.
-Gold sellers;
-IMC is a company that can't keep up with their word. I.e.: saying that they'll allow server transfers in the future when regional servers are released. Then, they say transfer won't be possible.
-Bugged quests;
-A lot of crashing during cutscenes;
-And much more.

I could stay here forever listing the cons, but they're simply too many. Sorry.

I stopped playing this game a long time ago (after 450 hours) and got back to it recently for a few days... Good Lord, what a mess they made with the character building experience in this game... 

 - They completely changed the class system, really late game classes, difficult to get, can now be achieved in the first class advancement. You get skills which used to be there to help you catch up with the rising dificulty of the game, but now are completely broken at the start, because they were not made thinking of early game content;
 - The stats now are automatic, which makes me wonder why they even show them anymore;
 - Some skills required consumable material to cast, which added a layer to the game. That's gone now, although you can still buy the items at the class trainers;

Tree of Savior, from my experience, doesn't have a whole lot of unique content, so character building is a big part of it, and they took a lot of the challenge of it. To me, this game is pretty much ruined. In its initial state, I would totally recomend it, I've had a lot of fun with it. The way it is now, there's no way, it's just a waste of time. Unless you love PvP comment, which I can't say a single word about (I'm not a pvp fan, so I have no idea what the pvp is like), or if the end game content is incredible, which I highly doubt, I wouldn't recommend playing it.
